 "notes": "The list starts at the foot of p. 27 (n42.jpg, 23 rows, Longstone to Corton) and continues at the head of p. 28 (n43.jpg, 13 rows, Languard Point to Hanois). n40, n41 and n44 don't carry it: n40 is p. 25, East Coast of Scotland text. The list stops at Hanois. The next list on p. 28 (Dungeness, Royal Sovereign Shoals, Beachy Head, Owers, St Katherine's, Nab) belongs to the South East Coast and is not included.\n\nLayout: two columns, the station and its type on the left and the keeper on the right, joined by dotted leaders. The 'printed' field leaves the leaders out and puts two spaces between the columns. Types are printed in small capitals (L.H., L.V.) and are written here as plain capitals. 'Nil.' is printed in italics, so it appears as _Nil._ in 'printed' and 'other'. Nothing in the list has a station number, mark or light character. All the scans were clear, and no word was hard to read.\n\nThe row count agrees with the text above the list. It says schedules went to 36 stations and returns came from 30. There are 36 rows, and 6 of them are Nil (Tees Breakwater, Hasbro' L.H., Newarp, Orfordness, Corton, Tongue).\n\nChoices made in the fields:\n- Each row ends with a full stop. I dropped it from the keepers' names, so 'Thomas O. Hall.' becomes 'Thomas O. Hall'.\n- Where two people are named with 'and' (e.g. 'W. Stock and A. Bearling'), each has a full name, so they are listed as separate keepers.\n- For Spurn L.V. and East Side L.V. the keeper column says 'The Principal (no signature).' That names no one, so it goes in 'other' and keepers is empty.\n- The 5 in 'Tees, 5 Buoy' is part of the vessel's name (the No. 5 buoy light-vessel), not a map number. 'Farn, Inner,' is printed with commas; the name is given as 'Farn, Inner'.\n- Hanois L.H., Guernsey, is a Channel Islands light, but it is printed as the last row of this East Coast list. It is kept here with place 'Guernsey'.\n- There is no sub-heading inside the section, so coast is the section heading, 'EAST COAST OF ENGLAND'.\n\nSpellings copied as printed, not corrected: 'Farn' (Farne), 'Hasbro'' (Happisburgh), 'Llyn Wells' (Lynn Well L.V.), 'Languard Point' (Landguard), 'Orfordness' printed as one word. The surnames 'Perfrement' and 'Bearling' are clear in the scan and match the OCR, though both are unusual. Spurn and Hasbro' each have two rows, one L.H. and one L.V.; they are separate stations.",
